*   Operation: Matrix multiplication $C = A \times B$ where $A, B, C$ are $n \times n$ matrices.
    *   Algorithm used in the provided code:
        ```c
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) C[i*n + j] = 0.0;
            for (int k = 0; k < n; k++) {
                double a = A[i*n + k];
                for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)
                    C[i*n + j] += a * B[k*n + j];
            }
        }
        ```
    *   This is the "IKJ" order of matrix multiplication, which is cache-friendly because the innermost loop iterates over $j$, and both $C[i*n + j]$ and $B[k*n + j]$ are accessed sequentially.
